# SDL2 runtime libraries

The browser export overlays SDL2 into `wine32.zip` and `wine64.zip`. Each
architecture includes Debian Bookworm `libsdl2-2.0-0` version
`2.26.5+dfsg-1` and the transitive ELF libraries that were absent from the
runtime ZIPs when this set was assembled.

## Source packages

| Architecture | Debian package URL | Version | SHA-256 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| amd64 | <https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/libs/libsdl2/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_amd64.deb> | `2.26.5+dfsg-1` | `9f97f2ccf78573d5327ba34c9553952520f9d4da5af2b390d919eabdac69c546` |
| i386 | <https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/libs/libsdl2/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_i386.deb> | `2.26.5+dfsg-1` | `ba21afbcaffdf4b2adc4d113fcc3e0d398d6e267e169aa304409a33e05e05fd0` |

The additional missing hard dependencies are `libXss.so.1`,
`libdecor-0.so.0`, `libdrm.so.2`, `libgbm.so.1`, `libsamplerate.so.0`,
`libwayland-client.so.0`, `libwayland-cursor.so.0`, `libwayland-egl.so.1`,
`libwayland-server.so.0`, and `libxkbcommon.so.0`. Their transitive
`DT_NEEDED` closure was checked against the Debian Bookworm library packages
and the existing runtime ZIPs.

## Refresh

Run this from the repository root. The SDL2 debs are pinned by URL and hash;
the Bookworm packages installed in the temporary container provide their
runtime dependencies. `install` dereferences the package symlinks so every
committed file is a regular shared object at its SONAME path.

```sh
set -euo pipefail
stage=/tmp/boxedwine-sdl2-bookworm
mkdir -p "$stage/debs"
curl -fL 'https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/libs/libsdl2/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_amd64.deb' -o "$stage/debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_amd64.deb"
curl -fL 'https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/libs/libsdl2/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_i386.deb' -o "$stage/debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_i386.deb"
printf '%s  %s\n' \
  '9f97f2ccf78573d5327ba34c9553952520f9d4da5af2b390d919eabdac69c546' "$stage/debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_amd64.deb" \
  'ba21afbcaffdf4b2adc4d113fcc3e0d398d6e267e169aa304409a33e05e05fd0' "$stage/debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_i386.deb" | sha256sum -c -
docker run --rm --platform linux/amd64 \
  -v "$PWD:/out" -v "$stage/debs:/debs:ro" debian:bookworm \
  bash -euxc '
    dpkg --add-architecture i386
    apt-get update -qq
    DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends \
      libsdl2-2.0-0:amd64 libsdl2-2.0-0:i386
    dpkg-deb -x /debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_amd64.deb /tmp/sdl2-amd64
    dpkg-deb -x /debs/libsdl2-2.0-0_2.26.5+dfsg-1_i386.deb /tmp/sdl2-i386
    libraries="libSDL2-2.0.so.0 libXss.so.1 libdecor-0.so.0 libdrm.so.2 libgbm.so.1 libsamplerate.so.0 libwayland-client.so.0 libwayland-cursor.so.0 libwayland-egl.so.1 libwayland-server.so.0 libxkbcommon.so.0"
    for arch in amd64 i386; do
      if [ "$arch" = amd64 ]; then triplet=x86_64-linux-gnu; sdl=/tmp/sdl2-amd64; else triplet=i386-linux-gnu; sdl=/tmp/sdl2-i386; fi
      mkdir -p "/out/tools/rootfs64/sdl2/$arch/usr/lib/$triplet"
      for library in $libraries; do
        if [ "$library" = libSDL2-2.0.so.0 ]; then source="$sdl/usr/lib/$triplet/$library"; else source="/usr/lib/$triplet/$library"; fi
        install -D -m 0644 "$source" "/out/tools/rootfs64/sdl2/$arch/usr/lib/$triplet/$library"
      done
    done
  '
```

## Committed shared objects

Each SHA-256 is over the regular file at the listed SONAME path. Both
architectures use the same 11 library names; the i386 and amd64 bytes differ.

| Library | amd64 SHA-256 | i386 SHA-256 |
